WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.082
In this video, you will put your own home on the map, so families can find your lights and drive by.

00:00:06.082 --> 00:00:09.064
You will add the address, a description, and photos.

00:00:09.064 --> 00:00:13.227
You need to be signed in to add a home, and in this video we already are.

00:00:13.227 --> 00:00:14.352
We start on the map.

00:00:15.251 --> 00:00:17.000
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:19.925 --> 00:00:22.442
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:24.531 --> 00:00:25.512
Then tap Allow.

00:00:29.245 --> 00:00:32.482
Now look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:32.482 --> 00:00:35.308
See your picture, or your initial, in a circle?

00:00:35.308 --> 00:00:40.075
That is your account menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:40.075 --> 00:00:40.487
Tap it.

00:00:42.135 --> 00:00:45.079
In the menu, tap Add an event, home or contest.

00:00:46.744 --> 00:00:50.798
That is where you add anything new: an event, a contest, or your own home.

00:00:51.498 --> 00:00:53.077
Now tap A lighting display.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:01:01.754
This is for showing off your own home, or a home you decorated for a customer, so families can drive by and see it.

00:01:02.458 --> 00:01:03.445
Who is posting?

00:01:03.445 --> 00:01:05.543
A homeowner is for your own home.

00:01:05.543 --> 00:01:09.059
A professional installer is for a home your company did.

00:01:09.059 --> 00:01:12.144
We are a homeowner, so tap A homeowner, then Next.

00:01:14.665 --> 00:01:16.052
Type the name to show.

00:01:16.052 --> 00:01:20.394
This is the name people see on the map, for example, the Garcia family.

00:01:20.394 --> 00:01:22.686
It does not have to be your full name.

00:01:24.477 --> 00:01:26.487
Did a company install your lights?

00:01:26.487 --> 00:01:30.449
If one did, you can name them, and your home links to their profile.

00:01:30.449 --> 00:01:32.861
We did it ourselves, so tap No, then Next.

00:01:35.377 --> 00:01:37.322
Which season are your lights for?

00:01:37.322 --> 00:01:41.670
Visitors pick a season on the map, so choose the one your lights belong to.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.100
Tap Christmas, then Next.

00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:49.330
Type a display name, and tell us what makes your home special.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.511
Is it the music, the animation, the number of lights?

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:55.987
Families read this to decide whether it is worth the drive.

00:01:59.568 --> 00:02:00.575
Add the address.

00:02:00.575 --> 00:02:07.568
This is where the pin goes, and visitors see it so they can drive by, so only add an address you want people to visit.

00:02:10.311 --> 00:02:16.576
Tell families when the lights are on, and how to enjoy them, like drive by, walk by, or where to park.

00:02:16.576 --> 00:02:20.530
Good directions make for happier visitors, and happier neighbors.

00:02:22.317 --> 00:02:23.028
Add photos.

00:02:23.028 --> 00:02:25.397
Take them at night, with the lights on.

00:02:25.397 --> 00:02:28.418
The first photo is the cover people see on the map.

00:02:31.296 --> 00:02:34.176
Finally, check everything, and tap Put it on the map.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:41.567
Your home usually goes on the map right away, for any family in Southern California to find.

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:46.457
If it is held for a quick check, it appears once the site owner has looked it over.

00:02:47.368 --> 00:02:49.373
Next up: Find lights near you.
